# Edit-sheet modals

For draft/edit sheets that explain a scoped change (payment options, automations, details, scheduled reminder, and similar):

1. Use `Modal` from `./ui` with:
   - `title` — short action title (e.g. "Edit Automations")
   - `subtitle` — centered intro copy (rendered as headline 6; **do not** hand-roll `type-headline-6` under the title)
   - `maxWidthClass="max-w-3xl"`
   - `zClass="z-[220]"` when opened over a draft/preview surface

2. **Do not** put a separate centered subtitle paragraph in `children`. Pass it as `subtitle` so title/subtitle spacing stays consistent (`mt-4` above the title block, `space-y-5` between title and subtitle, `mb-10` below before body).

3. Body content goes in `children` only (forms, lists, controls). Footer actions stay on Modal’s Save/Cancel.

```tsx
<Modal
  title="Edit Example"
  subtitle="Short explanation of what this change affects."
  maxWidthClass="max-w-3xl"
  zClass="z-[220]"
  confirmLabel="Save"
  onConfirm={save}
  onClose={onClose}
>
  {/* fields only */}
</Modal>
```
